pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Truth: SATISFIABLE. x1 + ~x1 == 1 >= -9223372036854775808 for either value of x1.
% Unfixed: normalizing the row cancels the opposite literals and lowers the degree
% by 1; the unchecked `-=` wraps i64::MIN to i64::MAX, so the trivially true input
% row is stored as the empty contradiction and `conclusion UNSAT : 1` is accepted.
f 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 1 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
